<title>USA: TABLE -- Wainoco Oil Q2 net income rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE -- Wainoco Oil Q2 net income rises.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>WAINOCO OIL CORPORATION</p>
<p>				 Six Months Ended  Three Months Ended</p>
<p>						June 30,     June 30,</p>
<p>					1997     1996     1997     1996</p>
<p> Revenues		     $185,900 $175,886 $ 96,330 $100,320</p>
<p> Operating income (loss)     3,471    2,920    9,045    5,921</p>
<p> Net income (loss)	     9,661  (3,705)   18,140    1,737</p>
<p>Income (loss) from continuing</p>
<p>   operations per share     (0.20)   (0.21)     0.17     0.06</p>
<p> Income (loss) per share	0.35   (0.14)     0.66     0.06</p>
<p>Average shares outstanding</p>
<p>				    27,337   27,256   27,415   27,330</p>
<p>REFINING</p>
<p>Operations (bpd)</p>
<p>   Total charges		40,493   40,184   42,341   42,296</p>
<p>   Gasoline yields	    16,860   17,318   16,456   16,969</p>
<p>   Distillate yields	  13,559   13,369   13,676   14,169</p>
<p>   Total sales		  39,987   38,744   41,848   40,910</p>
<p>Operating Margins (per bbl)</p>
<p>  Revenues			 25.51    24.86    25.06    26.87</p>
<p>  Material costs		 20.76    20.20    18.88    21.10</p>
<p>  Refined product margin	4.75     4.66     6.18     5.77</p>
<p>Operating costs excluding</p>
<p>    depreciation		  3.33     3.21     2.98     3.26</p>
<p>  Net margin			1.42     1.45     3.20     2.51</p>
<p>Light/Heavy crude spread</p>
<p>   (per bbl)			3.40     2.56     3.32     2.58</p>
<p>NOTE: Co says during quarter recorded $23.3 million gain on sale of Canadian assets.</p>
<p>Co says good demand and prices for refined products in Rockie Mountain region and lower crude costs increased refined product spread to $6.18 per barrel from $5.77 per barrel during Q2 1996.</p>
<p>KEY TERMS</p>
<p>bp =  barrels per day</p>
<p>bb =  barrel</p>
<p>(Financial information in thousands except per share)</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1700</p>
</text>
